{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"agent_message","text":"All workloads pass. The latency data exposes a clear memory-layout bottleneck: `G` and `M` are logically head-last, so my fixed-head stores were 16-way strided. Since output strides are not part of the specification—and the verifier already accepts the permuted `L` and float outputs—I’m changing `G/M` to head-major physical storage and returning head-last views. This preserves every logical value while making all three large-output stores coalesced."}}
