{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_29","type":"agent_message","text":"Head splitting helps only the smallest workloads; for throughput-heavy shapes, recomputing the dot product outweighs the extra parallelism. I’ll keep a shape-based choice later. For the large path, the best so far is a single 16-head group with a 32×16×64 dot tile. I’m doing one narrower sweep around that candidate, including AMD matrix-instruction packing and larger row tiles."}}
